      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "type": "llm",
      "param": {
        "system": "You are an expert curriculum designer. Create a comprehensive course syllabus with clear chapter structure. Each chapter should have a title and brief description.",
        "user": "Based on the following information, create a detailed course syllabus:\n\n**Learning Field**: {{#2.learning_field#}}\n**Learning Goals**: {{#2.learning_goals#}}\n**Learning Preferences**: {{#2.learning_preferences#}}\n**Daily Learning Duration**: {{#2.learning_duration#}}\n\nPlease provide:\n1. A list of 8-12 chapters covering the complete learning path\n2. Each chapter should have a clear title and 2-3 sentence description\n3. Format as a JSON array: [{\"title\": \"Chapter Title\", \"description\": \"Brief description\"}, ...]"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "type": "code",
      "param": {
        "variables": [["syllabus_text", ["text", "3"]]],
        "outputs": [["chapters", "array[object]"]],
        "code": "import json\n\ndef main(syllabus_text: str):\n    try:\n        # Try to parse the LLM response as JSON\n        chapters = json.loads(syllabus_text)\n        if not isinstance(chapters, list):\n            # Fallback if response isn't proper JSON array\n            lines = [line.strip() for line in syllabus_text.split('\\n') if line.strip()]\n            chapters = []\n            for i, line in enumerate(lines):\n                if line.startswith('**') or line.startswith('##'):\n                    title = line.replace('**', '').replace('##', '').strip()\n                    description = lines[i+1] if i+1 < len(lines) else \"\"\n                    chapters.append({\"title\": title, \"description\": description})\n        return {\"chapters\": chapters}\n    except:\n        # Final fallback\n        return {\"chapters\": [{\"title\": \"Introduction\", \"description\": \"Basic concepts\"}, {\"title\": \"Advanced Topics\", \"description\": \"Deep dive\"}]}"
      }
    },
